<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE-S.African expenditure budget for 1997/98.</title>
<headline>TABLE-S.African expenditure budget for 1997/98.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table lists the main expenditure items in the budget for 1997/98 presented by Finance Minister Trevor Manuel and the increases on the equivalent figures for the fiscal year ending on March 31:</p>
<p>    (rand bln)			1997/98	   1996/97   +/-</p>
<p>    State debt			39.643	    36.071    3.572</p>
<p>Improvement in conditions</p>
<p>    of service			 4.875	     7.481   -2.606</p>
<p>    Transfers to provinces	80.806	    73.873    6.933</p>
<p>    Central Statistical Serv	  85		 373    - 288</p>
<p>    Constitutional Developemnt     683	     1.016    - 333</p>
<p>    Health (national)		  358		 712    - 353</p>
<p>    Housing			    4.038	     1.575    2.463</p>
<p>    Public Works		     3.098	     2.823	275</p>
<p>    Defence			    9.579	    10.246    - 668</p>
<p>    Police			    11.919	     9.884    2.035</p>
<p>    Correctional serv (prisons)  3.320	     2.591	729</p>
<p>    State expenditure		1.022	     1.180    - 158</p>
<p>    Trade and industry	     3.049	     3.269    - 220</p>
<p>    Water and forestry	     2.143	     2.353    - 210</p>
<p>    Unallocated expenditure	2.074		 600    1.474</p>
<p>    All other budget votes	19.757	     19.545     211</p>
<p>    Subtotal budget/statutory  186.447	    173.590  12.856</p>
<p>    Standing appropriations	  300		   69     231</p>
<p>    TOTAL			    186.747	    173.659  13.087</p>
<p>NOTE: The expenditure figures for 1996/97 are as presented in last year's budget and do not include additional appropriations announced in February 1997.</p>
<p>-- Parliamentary newsroom +27 21 403-2502</p>
